      Marketplace {
        Description: "A pack of flat social media icons (38).\r\n\r\nContains all the usual ones like Twitter, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok...\r\n\r\nSee READ_ME for information.\r\n\r\nThere is an example to view all of them called \"Social Media Icon Pack 1 - Example\".\r\n\r\nIcons come from: iconarchive.com"
      }
      DirectlyPublished: true
    }
    Assets {
      Id: 11504945230836240875
      Name: "READ_ME"
      PlatformAssetType: 3
      TextAsset {
        Text: "--[[\r\n\tHi.\r\n\r\n\tJust a simple flat icon pack.  A few I had to modify that didn\'t have a background as\r\n\ttransparency isn\'t supported for screen shots.\r\n\r\n\tEach icon is 128 x 128 px but scaled down to 64 x 64.\r\n\r\n\tI made a template for each icon so it\'s easy to just drag and drop into the hierarchy.\r\n\r\n\tIcons come from: iconarchive.com\r\n\r\n\tThere is an example template you can drop in to see all of them.\r\n\r\n\tIf you would prefer to host the pack for yourself, you can download the texture atlas:\r\n\r\n\thttps://pixeldepth.net/core/icon-packs/social-media-icon-pack-1.png\r\n\r\n\t- Create a blank project\r\n\t- Publish game as unlisted\r\n\t- Use the image you downloaded as the screenshot\r\n\r\n\tTo use in a project:\r\n\r\n\t- Create UI Image\r\n\t- Set \"Game ID\" to the slug of your unlisted game (i.e \"9492fc/icon-pack-1\")\r\n\t- Select screenshot index \r\n\t- Set the size of the image and x / y offset\r\n]]"
      }
    }
    Assets {
      Id: 2074077888780800737
      Name: "Spacer_Client"
      PlatformAssetType: 3
      TextAsset {
        Text: "local container = script:GetCustomProperty(\"container\"):WaitForObject()\r\n\r\nlocal offset_x = 0\r\nlocal offset_y = 0\r\nlocal counter = 1\r\n\r\nfor i, c in ipairs(container:GetChildren()) do\r\n\tc.x = offset_x\r\n\tc.y = offset_y\r\n\r\n\toffset_x = offset_x + 70\r\n\r\n\tif(counter == 8) then\r\n\t\toffset_y = offset_y + 70\r\n\t\toffset_x = 0\r\n\t\tcounter = 0\r\n\tend\r\n\r\n\tcounter = counter + 1\r\nend"
      }
    }
